{%- comment -%}
  Language Switcher

  The switcher visitors see. Distinct from the floating locale switcher the
  CloudCannon Connector draws inside the Visual Editor, which is editor-only and
  never reaches the built site.

  Renders nothing unless Rosey is enabled and at least one locale is configured
  under `languages` in /rosey.yml.

  The original language is served from the site root because utils/rosey.js
  builds with --default-language-at-root, so its link is page.url unprefixed.
  Which language that IS comes from rosey.yml's `default_language` — it is not
  assumed to be English, so a Spanish-first site shows "ES" here for the root
  and lists "EN" alongside it as a translation.

  Every link carries data-rosey-ignore. Rosey rewrites root-relative hrefs to the
  current locale when it builds each locale's copy of the site; without the
  ignore, each link would be rewritten to point at the locale you are already in
  and the switcher would do nothing.

  data-rcc-ignore keeps the connector from swapping these labels when an editor
  previews a locale: a language switcher that renames its own options as you
  switch is unusable.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if rosey.enabled and rosey.languages.size > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="c-languageSwitcher flex items-center gap-2 text-sm"
    role="group"
    aria-label="Language"
    data-rcc-ignore
  >
    <a
      href="{{ page.url }}"
      data-rosey-ignore
      hreflang="{{ rosey.defaultLanguage }}"
      lang="{{ rosey.defaultLanguage }}"
      class="c-languageSwitcher__link uppercase hover:underline"
    >{{ rosey.defaultLanguage }}</a>
    {%- for locale in rosey.languages -%}
      <a
        href="/{{ locale }}{{ page.url }}"
        data-rosey-ignore
        hreflang="{{ locale }}"
        lang="{{ locale }}"
        class="c-languageSwitcher__link uppercase hover:underline"
      >{{ locale }}</a>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
